WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.870
Speaker 1: We have new economic numbers there,
pretty good new weekly jobless claims have

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:08.220
again hit a new pandemic era low.

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:11.040
The Department of Labor once a week releases
these numbers.

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:12.480
They released them this morning.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:19.860
Initial jobless claims for the week ending
April 10th, meaning last week, came in at

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:23.920
five hundred seventy six thousand new claims.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:30.789
This is both lower than the 700000 number
that was expected and also the lowest in the

00:00:30.789 --> 00:00:33.100
era of the pandemic.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:38.180
Continuing claims for the week ending, April
3rd, three point seven million.

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:42.309
The basically right on track with what was
expected.

00:00:42.309 --> 00:00:47.639
And these are numbers that are likely to continue
improving if we can keep vaccinating quickly.

00:00:47.639 --> 00:00:54.850
We've talked about how in some sense the unemployment
numbers are inversely correlated to vaccination.

00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:59.249
Of course, there's a whole bunch of other
factors, including local hotspots and state

00:00:59.249 --> 00:01:00.760
by state guidelines.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:05.470
What's going on in Texas is different than
what's going on in the state of Washington

00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:07.229
as as two examples.

00:01:07.229 --> 00:01:12.810
But if you look at the vaccination docx numbers,
those numbers continue to increase.

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:17.420
We're now up to three point three million
doses per day.

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:22.640
In another 40 days, things could be looking
quite good.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:29.420
It's quite plausible that by Memorial Day
you will see more states drop mask mandates.

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:31.520
I'm not advocating for or against that.

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:36.580
I'm sort of talking about the the perspective
that I think more and more governors are taking

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:37.580
here.

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:43.251
But short of debating that, for me, the lesson
here, there's probably a few lessons, but

00:01:43.251 --> 00:01:48.249
the best lesson here is the best economic
policy.

00:01:48.249 --> 00:01:54.220
The best way to protect and shield and recover
the economy during a pandemic has always been

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:55.780
to just deal with the virus.

00:01:55.780 --> 00:02:02.790
And what I mean by that is early on in March,
debates about flights and debates about freedom

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:09.410
and debates about masks and closures, quarantines
and the constitutionality of lockdowns and

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:18.200
all of that stuff, there has always been one
path, which is the most the more quickly you

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:26.180
deal with the virus, regardless of the debates
around freedom and constitutionality and whatever,

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:31.180
dealing with the virus most quickly will help
the economy.

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:32.520
And we have examples of it.

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:35.900
New Zealand did an incredible job dealing
with the virus.

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:40.660
They didn't need long debates over whether
to open or closed their mouth.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:42.270
So they just they did it.

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:43.270
They dealt with it.

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:47.450
And then they had long periods of normality
where much of the rest of the world was very

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:49.100
far from normality.

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:55.070
Israel, in terms of vaccination, Israel was
able to strike a deal early with Pfizer being

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:59.450
a country of only nine million people to get
enough doses for everybody in exchange for

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:02.440
sharing data with Pfizer.

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:03.910
Businesses are open in Israel.

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:09.950
Passover was almost completely normal in Israel
a couple of weeks ago, the entire time the

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:17.250
United States wasted time with conversations
that were being forced upon us by the right,

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:21.300
by the trumpet's, by the anti massacres, by
whoever else.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:25.810
And all along, the best medical policy was
the best economic policy.

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:26.810
That's what we learned.

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:30.160
And it is increasingly borne out in the data
that we get.

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:34.230
Had we figured out testing earlier, instead
of Trump saying we don't need this slowdown,

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:35.810
testing 15 cases will go to zero.

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:39.560
If we just figured out testing and were able
to contain it, we would have had a problem.

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:43.700
Of course we would have had a problem in a
country of 330 million people, but it wouldn't

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:45.730
have gotten as bad as it did.

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:48.200
The economy would have gotten better more
quickly.

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:52.730
Had we had competent leadership early, the
economy would have done better all along.

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:59.160
Other good indicators economically, by the
way, retail sales up about nine percent higher

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:00.620
in March.

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:01.840
That is significant.

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:08.400
A lot of it is coming from bars and restaurants
and other business areas.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:13.030
And then the result of all of this is the
stock market popping today, all time highs.

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:17.750
You're not seeing Joe Biden tweet endlessly
about it, but the Dow Jones Industrial Average

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:23.930
was up more than 200 points as of when I looked
at it half an hour ago, hit an all time high.

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:27.950
The S&amp;P 500 hitting an intraday record forever.

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:30.020
The forever record was hit today.

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:32.020
Nasdaq up one percent.

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:38.370
Of course, the economy is not the stock market,
but the point is all of it together confirms

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:41.230
that the better we do against the virus.

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:42.660
That's the economic policy.

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:48.270
It's not the debate between public health
policy and economic policy.

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:49.660
It's all the same.

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:50.950
The economy does better.

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:54.790
When we better deal with the virus, we better
deal with the virus.

00:04:54.790 --> 00:04:58.450
When we understand that we don't need to think
about the virus as.

00:04:58.450 --> 00:05:04.760
Separate and distinct from the economy, because
it all goes hand in hand, we'll hope for continued

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:06.590
improvement in the numbers.

00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:11.810
My belief is and again, I always make very
clear, I'm not coming up with this stuff on

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:12.810
my own.

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:16.540
I'm looking at the public health experts because
they are the experts.

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:23.750
It seems as though 40 days from now, numbers
will look significantly better and hopefully

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:25.900
as a result, economic numbers will.

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:26.220
As well

